@ifnottex
@node Top
@top EIGHTBOL Compiler Manual

This manual documents EIGHTBOL, a compiler that accepts programs written
in any of eight higher-level languages --- COBOL, BASIC, FORTRAN, Pascal,
Lua, Lingo, Objective-C, and SmallTalk --- and generates assembly code for
a wide variety of 8-bit and 16-bit microprocessors, including the 6502,
65c02, 65c816, HuC6280, RP2A03, cp1610, Z80, SM83, m68k, i286, ARM7, and
F8.

The manual is organized in the manner of the classic Programmer's
Reference Guides published for the Commodore VIC-20, 64, and 128, with a
dedicated chapter for each language, a chapter describing the abstract
syntax tree (AST) EIGHTBOL uses internally, and a chapter describing the
application binary interface (ABI) and assembler syntax for each
supported processor.

